## Context

The author agreed two tracks: a monthly public observatory and three academic contributions (JETP data paper, short historical comparison, long political economy with Christophe). The shared question is where JETPs stand and whether they accelerated project preparation and financing. Construction comparisons are premature.

Plan: `conception/jetp-observatory-and-papers-plan.md`. Programme tracker.

## First test

Integration acceptance exercise: follow one country total to project events and source locators, then reproduce a paper result from the exact frozen edition. A mismatched release, missing source or unsupported causal claim must fail review.

## Actions

Coordinate children 0726–0733 in the dependency order in the plan. Reuse 0715–0722 and 0711; do not duplicate collection or turn 0723 into a prerequisite. Record feasibility-led scope changes. This tracker remains open through an integration review.

The first programme milestone is now **M1**, accepted in two bounded steps:
[[0832]] published the four frozen country inventories without fusion; M1a itself is redefined by [[0834]] (2026-09-17): the MVP explores the data in three stages, documents, structured extraction and reconciled facts, with South Africa and Viet Nam as acceptance cases;
[[0833]] / M1b, accepted on 2026-10-01 (author decision, interactive), is an
acceptance milestone on the ontology v2 contract: D4 over the lines of the
four M1a documents, accepted referents and relations each citing their
justification lines and a decision row, every unaccepted proposal kept as a
candidate row (formerly `possible_match`), separate, not in force and
counted, and the ontology in force frozen as O v1. Monthly refresh, source
watching and match resolution begin only after this base (the milestone that
carries them was renamed on 2026-09-29: see the next section).

## Milestones after M1 (redefined 2026-09-29, amended 2026-10-01)

Author decision, interactive. The instrument, then the measurement, then its
operation.

- **M2, the instrument.** An extraction pipeline that works on every document
  held. Normative text: `docs/jetp-requirements.md` § 2.2,
  `docs/jetp-extraction.md` § 13 and `docs/jetp-operation.md` § 12 (spec v1,
  tag `jetp-spec-v1`). It includes the replay of the 254 extracted documents,
  comparator records replayed by ingestion run under the count control
  (extraction § 6.2); autonomous assisted reading of the one-off documents
  by two blind local readers and a hosted arbiter, calibrated on held-out
  reference answers, nothing queued for the author (extraction § 6.3);
  transcription of the held scan (§ 6.4); budgets, secrets, run reports and
  the run-output gate (operation §§ 4 to 8); and the one-way upload of the
  document bytes to Zotero with a restore test (operation § 9; author
  decision 2026-10-01, D2). M2 targets the register as frozen at 392
  documents (369 with a snapshot). Tracker [[1500]], phases M2.0 to M2.4.
- **M3a, discover and freeze.** Normative text: `docs/jetp-collection.md`
  (spec v1), whose § 5 fixes the stopping rule (2 % yield with a one-document
  floor, two quiet rounds in different channel classes, known-item recovery
  of at least 36 of 40) and leaves only the date and effort caps to the
  campaign's declaration; § 12 lists what M3a produces. Overlap with M2
  (author decision 2026-10-01, D3): the protocol declaration ([[1877]]) and
  the sealed known-item list ([[1878]]) may start now. Pilot rule: the
  campaign begins with a pilot round on a stratified sample (country ×
  channel class), quality-checked by a non-author checker, before it scales
  up. Sketch of the rest, to be ticketed when [[1877]] is accepted: the M3a
  storage tables ([[1871]], filed); the discovery campaign, per-country
  sections under one stopping rule; the secondary-to-primary pass, whose
  rounds count in the stopping rule (collection § 7) and so run within the
  campaign, not after it; the collection report, the freeze and the author's
  acceptance of the recall estimate and the unreachable list before M3b
  starts.
- **M3b, extract, reconcile, release.** Normative text:
  `docs/jetp-extraction.md` § 11, `docs/jetp-fusion.md`,
  `docs/jetp-results.md` § 13 (spec v1). Sketch, to be ticketed with M3a:
  extract the documents new since M2 with the M2 pipeline; the M3b storage
  slice ([[1872]], filed); reconcile with CRS and IATI ([[0721]]), which
  have no precedence of their own, closeness to the event being the first
  consideration of a judgement, never an automatic rank (fusion § 5); join
  events, assets and outcomes ([[0723]]); build the release (`release_id`
  `YYYY-MM`, descriptor, deposit, correction path `YYYY-MM-rN`, the two
  match thresholds set by the author before release; results §§ 3 to 9).
- **M4, operation.** Scheduled refresh, link-rot, the pass launcher, shared code
  for AEDIST; the recurring machinery, whose deterministic part is checked by
  replay over the M3 release ([[1141]], [[1184]], weekly cadence of [[1140]]).
  Also the move of the document store to a dedicated Zotero group library
  ([[1510]] tracker, [[1511]] Viet Nam pilot; author, 2026-09-29: "Zotero
  storage smells like M4 work"); the one-way upload of the bytes and its
  restore test are M2 ([[1712]]; author decision 2026-10-01, D2). Every acquisition writes through the single
  function of [[1184]], the storage seam. The shared PDF text layer of
  [[1512]] is taken up earlier, in M2, by [[1508]].
  Rule of two: shared code is extracted to `libs/` when a second consumer runs
  on it, not before.

## Exit criteria

- [x] M1a accepted: the MVP explores documents, extractions and facts end to end on the SA and VN acceptance cases ([[0834]]); the frozen inventories of [[0832]] are its input, not its result
- [x] M1b bounded catalogue accepted without changing M1a or resolving candidate rows (formerly `possible_match`); accepted 2026-10-01 ([[0833]])
- [ ] M2 accepted: the extraction pipeline replays the 254 extracted documents and has run over all documents held ([[1500]])
- [ ] M3a accepted: registry frozen at a published cutoff, with protocol, recall estimate and unreachable list
- [ ] M3b released: dataset extracted, reconciled with CRS and IATI, joined, citing its `release_id`
- [ ] Children 0726–0733 delivered, or scope changes explicitly adjudicated
- [ ] Public observatory and repeatable monthly editions operational
- [ ] Citable dataset and three reviewable manuscripts linked to frozen releases
- [ ] Integration review checks source traceability, reproducibility and separation of observation from inference

## Validation

Apply the repository gates for the actual diff. Code work starts with the failing
fixture above; prose/data work records the documentary acceptance check. Preserve
source evidence and report limits rather than manufacturing a successful result.

